  "summary": "Traditional Japanese lacquerware from Wajima known for its durability and the unique makie technique using gold and silver powder.",
  "description": "Features multiple layers of lacquer applied over a cloth foundation, often decorated with intricate gold and silver designs. Developed in the Edo period, Wajima lacquerware is distinguished by its exceptional durability and the sophisticated techniques used in its creation, particularly the nuri-e technique where designs are drawn with lacquer before being sprinkled with metal powder.",
